<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 2 September, from 31 BCE to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mark-antony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">31 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,995 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Octavian defeats Antony and Cleopatra at Actium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Octavian's fleet under Agrippa defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Cleopatra off Actium in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Their flight to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> left Octavian, soon to be Augustus, master of the Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1666 CE <span class="tih-ago">360 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Fire of London breaks out in Pudding Lane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire broke out in Thomas Farriner's bakery and raged for four days, destroying some 13,200 houses, 87 churches and old St Paul's Cathedral. Wren's rebuilding transformed the City.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1792 CE <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The September Massacres begin in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fearing a Prussian advance and a plot among prisoners, crowds broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> prisons and killed some 1,100 to 1,400 inmates over five days. The massacres foreshadowed the Terror.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan signs the instrument of surrender aboard USS Missouri</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese envoys signed the formal surrender in Tokyo Bay before General MacArthur and Allied representatives. The ceremony officially ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uss-missouri">USS Missouri</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 CE <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">CBS Evening News becomes America's first half-hour network newscast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Walter Cronkite's evening news on CBS expanded from 15 to 30 minutes, opening with an interview with President Kennedy. NBC followed within a week, setting the format of US network news.</p></div></li></ol>
